project KSHIAI_BATTLE_FIT_GAP:
  version 6
  title "Close v0.5.1 battle pipeline Fit and Gap findings"
  description |
    Implement the accepted battle-fit-gap backlog while keeping canonical world
    state character cognition actual speech public rendering narration and
    result authority separate. Use origin HEAD v0.5.1 at commit 206a1b0 as the
    analysis and integration baseline. Merge the narrator boundary first, then
    close perception action causality timing and compatibility gaps. After
    acceptance, safely classify and clean obsolete integration artifacts.
  as_of 2026-08-05
  duration_unit day
  finish REPOSITORY_CLEAN

resource DEV:
  title "Developer"
  capacity 1

milestone FIT_GAP_REVIEWED:
  title "Fit and Gap requirements and backlog recorded"
  state reached

milestone NARRATOR_READY:
  title "Character-authored speech and presentation-only narration ready"

milestone RULES_READY:
  title "Timing and adjudication decisions accepted"

milestone WORLD_MODEL_READY:
  title "Coarse canonical world and state model ready"

milestone PROFILE_GROUNDED:
  title "Character self profile and narrator identity grounding ready"

milestone PERCEPTION_BASE_READY:
  title "Initial and continuous perception ready"

milestone PERCEPTION_READY:
  title "Apparent identity and speech perception ready"

milestone ACTIONS_READY:
  title "Observer-safe feasible actions and revalidation ready"

milestone CAUSALITY_READY:
  title "World interference and conscious or unconscious effects ready"

milestone TIMELINE_READY:
  title "Side-neutral temporal resolution ready"

milestone RESULT_READY:
  title "Canonical result adjudication ready"

milestone PHASES_READY:
  title "Prologue normal turn and aftermath contracts aligned"

milestone COMPATIBILITY_READY:
  title "Legacy battle compatibility ready"

milestone GAP_ACCEPTED:
  title "Battle pipeline gaps accepted"

milestone REPOSITORY_CLEAN:
  title "Repository branches and workspaces safely cleaned"

task T_NARRATOR FIT_GAP_REVIEWED -> NARRATOR_READY:
  title "Make narration presentation-only and source public speech from characters"
  description |
    Close BL-001 BL-010 and BL-011 for narration. Amend the requirements and
    role boundary so isolated character agents own actual speech. Pass only
    accepted character speech to the narrator, allow placement and
    punctuation-only surface styling, reject invention or factual and intent
    changes, and fall back to the exact source line. Preserve source side and
    speaker, interleave speech at narrator-selected boundaries, support legacy
    narrative blocks, and never write public rendering back into private agent
    state. Remove public narrator prose from turn-limit referee input, replace it
    with bounded committed turn facts, then use a separate narrator call with the
    immutable raw judgment and recent public prose to frame a server-rendered
    canonical verdict line. Leave full result-factor coverage to T_ADJUDICATION.
    Apply the same no-invention rule to normal turns prologue and aftermath. Add
    contract provider service and UI-order regression tests plus a narrator-style
    non-feedback check.
  duration 2d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_RULES NARRATOR_READY -> RULES_READY:
  title "Accept side-neutral timing and canonical result rules"
  description |
    Close BL-002 and BL-003. Decide full simultaneity speed ordering or
    initiative buckets and record initiative inputs ties mutual incapacity
    interruption defense movement object conflicts and seeded randomness.
    Preserve the accepted two-stage turn-limit boundary: an independent semantic
    adjudicator decides from canonical facts, then the narrator presents the
    immutable judgment using public prose only as style continuity. Record this
    decision and update remaining conflicting requirements.
  duration 1d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_WORLD_MODEL RULES_READY -> WORLD_MODEL_READY:
  title "Define a coarse canonical position state and relation model"
  description |
    Close BL-020 without implementing exact coordinate physics. Add bounded
    structured relative distance presence exposure occlusion orientation
    sensory physical and mental states plus held worn attached and usable object
    relations. Define server-owned transitions and invariants shared by
    perception feasible actions causal effects and temporal resolution.
  duration 3d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_PROFILE_GROUNDING WORLD_MODEL_READY -> PROFILE_GROUNDED:
  title "Ground character self identity separately from narrator rendering"
  description |
    Close BL-012. Preserve the reported gender and self-profile drift as an
    unresolved provenance question because the example predates the narrator
    boundary and role-specific outputs are unavailable. Give each character
    agent a frozen complete own-profile anchor and state that canonical profile
    facts override contradictory private continuity while null facts remain
    unknown. Give prologue normal-turn and aftermath narrators a separate
    rendering-only identity anchor sufficient to avoid misgendering without
    writing it into cognition or leaking counterpart-private facts through a
    character-limited view. Add independent fixtures for character output and
    narrator output including explicit gender null gender multiple self names
    and nonhuman or appearance-atypical profiles.
  duration 2d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_PERCEPTION_BASE PROFILE_GROUNDED -> PERCEPTION_BASE_READY:
  title "Build realistic initial perception and explicit access continuity"
  description |
    Close BL-021 and BL-022. Derive initial A and B frames from setup and the
    coarse world so an ordinarily exposed counterpart is accessible without
    leaking unestablished identity. Retain current access when no new evidence
    arrives and lower it only through committed hiding disappearance occlusion
    absence or observer impairment transitions. Keep identity memory independent
    from current access and cover provider and projection failures.
  duration 3d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_PERCEPTION_APPARENT PERCEPTION_BASE_READY -> PERCEPTION_READY:
  title "Represent apparent identity and project actual speech per observer"
  description |
    Close BL-023 and BL-024. Separate canonical identity from perceived form
    suspected identity confidence and private belief for transformation disguise
    illusion and hallucination. Commit character-authored utterances as world
    events and project heard partial misunderstood unattributed or unheard speech
    through distance occlusion noise hearing consciousness and language state.
    Never use the public rendered line as a character observation.
  duration 3d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_ACTIONS PERCEPTION_READY -> ACTIONS_READY:
  title "Compute observer-safe feasible actions and revalidate intentions"
  description |
    Close BL-030 and BL-031. Compute available actions from canonical resources
    position state targets objects and scene constraints while exposing only
    observer-safe labels and choices to each character. Revalidate chosen intent
    after temporal conflicts and commit failure partial execution or an
    epistemically safe fallback without reading hidden opponent totals.
  duration 3d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_CAUSALITY ACTIONS_READY -> CAUSALITY_READY:
  title "Connect world objects states and effects to causal mechanics"
  description |
    Close BL-040 and BL-041. Make scene entities relations and effects constrain
    targets feasibility coefficients and state transitions through structured
    rules. Apply unperceived causes to canonical outcomes without revealing them
    and project only consequences that the observer can notice. Cover object and
    character interference plus conscious and unconscious influence fixtures.
  duration 3d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_TIMELINE CAUSALITY_READY -> TIMELINE_READY:
  title "Implement and prove the accepted fair temporal resolver"
  description |
    Close BL-050 and BL-051. Implement the accepted initiative and simultaneity
    rules without fixed Side A priority, use one turn-start snapshot for each
    simultaneous bucket, merge conflicts atomically, and preserve valid mutual
    incapacity. Add A and B swap metamorphic tests for equal and unequal speed
    mutual effects interruption movement and shared object conflicts.
  duration 3d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_ADJUDICATION TIMELINE_READY -> RESULT_READY:
  title "Derive turn-limit results from canonical records"
  description |
    Close BL-060. Remove public narration and rendered speech from result input.
    Complete the accepted independent semantic adjudication contract over
    committed actions effects state transitions and world impact, followed by a
    presentation-only narrator call that may see recent public narration. Prove
    that narration style provider timeout paraphrase and empty public prose
    cannot change winner finish reason rating input or canonical reason facts.
  duration 2d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_PHASES RESULT_READY -> PHASES_READY:
  title "Align prologue normal turn and aftermath authority contracts"
  description |
    Close BL-070. Apply the same actual-speech cognition perception narration
    and no-feedback boundaries to setup normal turns terminal turns and
    aftermath. Ensure the first character decision consumes initial perception
    and that no specialized narrator call invents speech or canonical outcomes.
  duration 2d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_COMPAT PHASES_READY -> COMPATIBILITY_READY:
  title "Migrate legacy battle perception and speech continuity safely"
  description |
    Close BL-080. Define deterministic reads and next-save migration for legacy
    identification access lastSpeech narrative blocks and missing world state.
    Preserve historical display while preventing old public rendering from
    becoming new private cognition. Verify bounded retention privacy failure and
    rollback-safe database compatibility.
  duration 2d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_ACCEPT COMPATIBILITY_READY -> GAP_ACCEPTED:
  title "Accept gap closure across mock XAI and fallback paths"
  description |
    Close BL-090. Run fixed setup perception speech world-action unconscious
    influence side-swap mutual-incapacity narration-independence and legacy
    fixtures. Review all prompts DTOs logs and persistence for hidden identity
    totals locations private state control IDs and narrator feedback. Obtain live
    XAI primary evidence then run tests typecheck build llmthink review and PERT
    checks before marking the project complete.
  duration 2d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_CLEANUP GAP_ACCEPTED -> REPOSITORY_CLEAN:
  title "Safely clean obsolete branches stashes and worktrees"
  description |
    Inventory local and remote branches stashes and linked worktrees after final
    acceptance. For each candidate prove its commits and reusable file changes
    are integrated or explicitly preserved and verify the published destination
    SHA before deletion. Present any ambiguous or unmerged target for explicit
    confirmation; never delete it by age name or apparent similarity alone.
    Remove only confirmed obsolete artifacts, prune stale references without
    touching active work, and finish with the intended main branch and every
    retained worktree clean. Record what was removed and what WIP was retained.
  duration 1d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

